From 42659146ca31cf23ceb0d72c1d2ca5949f20590e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:18:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] pipeline: mtkcamraw: Add the MediaTek MT6878 hardware
 ISP replay pipeline

The mtk-camraw-mt6878 kernel driver runs the RAW/YUV engines of the
MT6878 image signal processor with the command queue of captured
requests and delivers the processed picture (NV21, one fixed size) on a
video node in a media device of its own. The sensor and the sensor
interface that feed it are in the media device of the CAMSV engine of
the same CSI port; the node names that sensor interface entity as its
input, and its crop bounds give the sensor frame the captured requests
need.

The handler takes both media devices, sets the sensor and the sensor
interface to that mode, streams the video node (the driver starts the
sensor interface and the sensor), and drives the sensor's exposure, gain
and vertical blanking through DelayedControls, timed by the node's frame
start events. Exposure is decided by the mtkcamraw IPA from a luma
histogram the handler takes from every picture.

The camera is offered only when the driver has its captured requests
loaded (the node reports a picture format); otherwise both media devices
are released and the simple pipeline handler keeps the sensor with its
software ISP. Listed before simple, the hardware path wins when it is
available; LIBCAMERA_PIPELINES_MATCH_LIST=simple selects the software
ISP for that sensor.

The picture is offered with the line pitch as its width (1472 x 1088
for a 1450 x 1088 picture, the driver fills the padding columns black):
consumers that ignore the stride (seen through PipeWire) sheared it.
pipelines: mtkcamraw: full_pitch: false in the configuration file offers
the picture width with the stride instead.

Neither the sensor nor the replayed lists can flip or rotate, so the
configuration reports the sensor's mounting orientation and applications
rotate. The IPA is started from the exposure and gain the sensor holds and
returns its start values (inside its limits), which go to the sensor,
blanking first, before it streams; a frame the driver returns with an
error gets no statistics.

Signed-off-by: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
